---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { Code } from "astro:components";

title: "Download & Install";
description: "Install Umi‑Time via npm, CDN, or GitHub releases.";
---

<Base title="Install Umi‑Time">
  <div class="umi-region umi-pad">
    <main class="page page-install">
      <header class="page-header">
        <h1>Install Umi‑Time</h1>
        <p>
          <p>
            The umi-time library supports the complete Umi‑Time architecture,
            including universal Umi‑Time values, longitude‑based local
            interpretation, and optional solar context calculations.
          </p>
        </p>
        <p>
          Umi‑Time is available via npm, CDN, and GitHub releases. Choose the
          method that fits your workflow.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- NPM Install -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Install via npm</h2>
        <p>The recommended way to use Umi‑Time in production.</p>

        <Code code={`npm install umi-time`} lang="bash" theme="dracula" />

        <Code code={`pnpm add umi-time`} lang="bash" theme="dracula" />

        <Code code={`yarn add umi-time`} lang="bash" theme="dracula" />
      </section>

      <!-- CDN -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Use via CDN</h2>
        <p>Great for demos, prototypes, and quick experimentation.</p>

        <Code
          code={`<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/umi-time/dist/umi-time.min.js"></script>`}
          lang="html"
          theme="dracula"
        />

        <Code
          code={`<script src="https://unpkg.com/umi-time/dist/umi-time.min.js"></script>`}
          lang="html"
          theme="dracula"
        />
      </section>

      <!-- Minimal Working Example -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Minimal Working Example</h2>
        <p>
          Copy‑paste this into an <code>index.html</code> file to verify everything
          works.
        </p>

        <Code
          code={`<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <body>
    <h2>Umi‑Time Minimal Example</h2>

    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/umi-time/dist/umi-time.min.js"></script>
    <script>
      // Create a Layer 1 Umi‑Time value from the current UTC moment
      const umi = new UmiTime(new Date());

      // Output the canonical textual representation
      console.log(umi.format(UMI_EXTENDED));
    </script>
  </body>
</html>`}
          lang="html"
          theme="dracula"
        />
      </section>

      <section class="example">
        <h2>Package Contents</h2>
        <p>The npm package includes only the compiled distribution files:</p>

        <ul>
          <li><strong>dist/index.js</strong> — ES module build</li>
          <li><strong>dist/index.cjs</strong> — CommonJS build</li>
          <li><strong>dist/index.d.ts</strong> — TypeScript definitions</li>
          <li>
            <strong>dist/umi-time.min.js</strong> — Minified IIFE bundle for browsers
            (global <code>UmiTime</code>)
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Source files, tests, and documentation remain in the GitHub repository
          and are not included in the npm package.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Versioning -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>Versioning & Compatibility</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Stable version: <strong>1.x</strong></li>
          <li>Browser support: modern evergreen browsers</li>
          <li>
            Builds:
            <ul>
              <li>ES module build (ESM)</li>
              <li>CommonJS build (CJS)</li>
              <li>Minified bundle for browsers (IIFE)</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>Node: 18+</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- TypeScript -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>TypeScript Support</h2>
        <p>
          Umi‑Time ships with full TypeScript definitions. All public
          APIs—including
          <code>UmiTime</code>, solar‑context and solar‑geometry helpers, error
          types, and format constants—are strongly typed and included in the npm
          package via <code>dist/index.d.ts</code>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Links -->
      <section class="example">
        <h2>More Resources</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/api/">API Reference</a></li>
          <li><a href="/examples/">Examples & Demos</a></li>
          <li><a href="/getting-started/">Getting Started</a></li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://github.com/umi-time/umi-time/releases"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Releases</a
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Base>
